      "content": "I see what you mean about the methodology, but I'm worried that if we just talk about \"best practices,\" the reviewers will see that 5% and realize we failed our target. They're looking for heavy hitters. Is there a way to actually describe that 5% growth in a way that sounds like a major win? Like, can we frame it as something much more substantial or transformative so they don't question our effectiveness?",
